  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41301" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to small-scale dairy farmers, sheep herders and IDPs in northwest Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective to improve livelihoods and diets of crisis-affected vulnerable households, FAO aims to improve the productivity of dairy animals and enhance local vegetable production through the implementation of activities under four main outputs. This includes improved access to livestock services (artificial insemination and fertility treatments) and enhanced livestock breeding knowledge and skills to directly benefit 2 500 small-scale farmers and herders, as well as improved artificial insemination and fertility treatment skills for livestock service providers. In addition, 2 000 IDPs and women-headed host community households will improve their capacity for homestead vegetable production through training and input provision.</narrative>
  </description>
